        {
          "id": 932551603,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It was tools/check_typed_item_calls.py, which is already running on CI.  We could add --consecutive --label --mask, all of which output warnings that would not cause the job to fail.  The trouble is that there are lots of similar warnings that are actually fine.  Do you think we should?  The number of warnings for any given commit is likely to be small.",
